        "# Where You Grow Up Matters: Predicting Adult Income for Low-Income Children in the DC Region\n",
        "## Capstone Two: Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Project question:** Which neighborhood characteristics best predict how much children from low-income families earn as adults, across census tracts in the DC metro area (DC, Prince George's County, Arlington, Fairfax, and Alexandria)?\n",
        "\n",
        "**What this notebook does:** it starts from the cleaned file created in the Data Wrangling notebook (`data/processed/dc_region_clean.csv`) and works through: **1. Profile the data, 2. Look at every feature, 3. Hypotheses and statistical tests, 4. Relationships and visuals, 5. A second outcome, 6. Feature selection and engineering, 7. Answers to the four EDA questions.**\n",
        "\n",
        "**The four questions this notebook answers**\n",
        "1. Which variables best explain the project question?\n",
        "2. Do subgroups (state, county) differ?\n",
        "3. Which variables are strongly correlated with each other?\n",
        "4. Which statistical tests fit this data?\n",
        "\n",
        "**How to use this notebook**\n",
        "1. In Colab, upload `dc_region_clean.csv` (the final cell of the wrangling notebook saves it), or run the upload cell in Section 1.\n",
        "2. Run the cells from top to bottom.\n",
        "3. The cells labeled **Write-up note** are drafted in first person with the numbers this notebook produces. Read each one, confirm the numbers match your own output, and rewrite it in your own words.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Rubric check:** every feature investigated with visual and numeric means; Pearson correlations and other statistical methods to show relationship strength; data-supported decisions on which features to keep; a working, commented notebook uploaded in full to GitHub."
      ]
