      "source": [
        "### Do subgroups differ? (state and county)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Write-up note (hypotheses for the group tests):**\n",
        "- **H0:** the mean income rank is the same in DC, Maryland, and Virginia tracts.\n",
        "- **H1:** at least one state's mean income rank is different.\n",
        "\n",
        "I use a one-way **ANOVA** because I am comparing the means of three groups, and the **Kruskal-Wallis** test as a check because it does not assume normal data. If they are significant I use **Tukey's HSD** to see which pairs of states differ. I also report **eta-squared**, which is the share of the outcome's variation explained by group membership (the effect size)."
      ]
