        "The two outcomes are related (correlation -0.56): tracts where low-income children reach higher income ranks tend to have lower incarceration rates. The predictors that matter most for income rank also show up for incarceration, in the opposite direction (for example, share Black has r = 0.51 with incarceration, and single-parent share has r = 0.46). I will keep income rank as the main outcome. The incarceration rate is much noisier (many values sit near zero, and some were pushed negative by privacy noise), so I treat it as supporting evidence only."
      ]
    },
